OL,3,GNEWSAGene-edited soya beans show
OL,4,Apromise in UK trial
OL,5,
OL,6,FSoya beans could one day be grown
OL,7,Fcommercially in Britain after a
OL,8,Fgene-edited crop produced a healthy
OL,9,Fharvest in a trial in Warwickshire.
OL,11,FSoya is used as feed for animals such
OL,12,Fas cattle and chickens, but the UK
OL,13,Frelies heavily on imports because the
OL,14,Fcooler British climate means it is
OL,15,Fdifficult to grow the crop.
OL,17,FHowever, the Warwickshire trial,
OL,18,Fcarried out by US company Corteva, has
OL,19,Findicated that soya could be grown in
OL,20,Fthe West Midlands.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
